Effect does NOT include (not dispatch_allocated ?origin_availability). So dispatch_allocated remains true after dispatch! Similarly for execute_destination_dispatch and execute_schedule_dispatch. So dispatch_allocated persists, and dispatch_slot_available becomes true (slot becomes available). So we can have multiple candidates with dispatch_allocated true and each linked to the same slot? The allocate action sets candidate_dispatch_slot_linked and dispatch_allocated, and removes dispatch_slot_available. After execution, dispatch_slot_available becomes true again, but the candidate_dispatch_slot_linked remains? The effect of execute does not remove candidate_dispatch_slot_linked. So after dispatch, the candidate still has candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true and dispatch_allocated true, and slot becomes available again. Thus we can allocate slot to multiple candidates sequentially: each allocation consumes slot availability, sets dispatch_allocated and link; after dispatch, slot becomes available again, allowing another allocation. At the end, all four candidates will have dispatch_allocated true and candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true (since never removed). Good.

Thus we need to allocate slot, execute dispatch, repeat for each candidate.

Now we also need dispatch_ready for each candidate before allocation. dispatch_ready can be set via finalize actions (after validation) or via mark_*_availability_dispatch_ready actions for origin/destination availability. For shift candidates we will use finalize after sequence validation. For origin and destination availability, we have actions mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready which set dispatch_ready given origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready. So we need transport leg assembled and loading authorized before we can set dispatch ready for origin/destination.

Thus we need to assemble transport leg and authorize loading before we can mark origin/destination availability dispatch ready.

Thus order: prepare origin/destination, load/unload payload to get locked/confirmed/nodes ready, then assemble transport leg, authorize loading, then mark origin/destination dispatch ready, then allocate slot and execute dispatch for origin and destination.

For shift candidates, we need to go through loading verification, clearance, service window attachment, route validation, finalize, allocate slot, execute dispatch.

Now we need to also achieve candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (we will assign). Also candidate_skill_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha.

We also need candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha (we will assign).

We also need candidate_finalized shift_candidate_beta (will be set by finalize action).

We also need candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta (from verification).

We also need candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta (from staging).

We also need candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta (from prepare).

We also need candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (attach).

We also need candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma (allocate vehicle).

We also need candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_beta dispatch_slot_alpha (via allocate then dispatch).

We also need dispatch_ready shift_candidate_beta (from finalize).

We also need dispatched shift_candidate_beta (from execute).

Now for origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha:

We need candidate_prepared (via confirm_candidate_preparedness) requiring vehicle_allocated and candidate_task_profile_linked.

We need vehicle_allocated: origin_availability_alpha already has vehicle_unit_alpha allocated. Good. destination_availability_alpha need vehicle_unit_beta allocated.

We need candidate_task_profile_linked for both to route_task_profile_alpha.

We need candidate_vehicle_linked: origin already linked to vehicle_unit_alpha (init). destination will be linked after allocation.

We need candidate_dispatch_slot_linked to dispatch_slot_alpha (via allocate then dispatch).

We need dispatch_allocated (via allocate then dispatch will keep true).

We need dispatch_ready (via mark_*_availability_dispatch_ready after transport leg assembled and loading authorized).

We need dispatched (via execute_*_dispatch after allocation).

We also need origin_node_occupied and destination_node_occupied (via load/unload payload). We'll do load then unload.

We also need origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready (via unload).

We also need origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed (via unload? Actually unload sets confirmed; load does not. After load/unload sequence we will have confirmed true.)

We also need origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked (load sets locked true; unload does not change locked, so remains true). Good.

Now we need to ensure we have cargo_available for loading. Initially cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha. After loading origin payload, cargo becomes unavailable. After loading destination payload, cargo becomes available again (since load_destination_payload effect includes cargo_available). Wait load_destination_payload effect: destination_node_occupied, destination_availability_locked, destination_payload_linked, not cargo_available. So loading destination payload makes cargo unavailable again. Actually both load actions remove cargo availability. So after loading origin, cargo unavailable; after loading destination, cargo still unavailable (since second load also removes). There is no unload action for destination? There is unload_destination_payload which adds cargo_available. So we could load origin, load destination, then unload destination to make cargo available again? But goal does not require cargo_available; it's not in goal. So we can leave cargo unavailable. However we need to load origin payload and destination payload to get nodes occupied and availability locked. After loading both, cargo unavailable twice (still unavailable). That's fine. We don't need to unload.

But we need origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready; those are set by unload actions, not load. So we need to unload after loading to get ready. However unload will make cargo available again and remove payload link. So we could load origin, unload origin (get origin ready, cargo available), then load destination, unload destination (get destination ready, cargo available again). At end cargo available. That's okay.

Thus we will do load_origin_payload, unload_origin_payload, load_destination_payload, unload_destination_payload.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_prepared and candidate_task_profile_linked for origin and destination before loading.

Now we need to ensure we have transport leg assembled and loading authorized before we can mark origin/destination dispatch ready.

Thus overall plan:

1. Prepare origin_availability_alpha:
   - attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (requires vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha true, route_task_profile_available assumed)
   - confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, candidate_task_profile_linked, not candidate_prepared)

2. Prepare destination_availability_alpha:
   - allocate_vehicle_unit destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta (requires candidate_created, not vehicle_allocated, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta)
   - attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
   - confirm_candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha

3. Prepare shift_candidate_beta:
   - allocate_vehicle_unit shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma (requires candidate_created, not vehicle_allocated, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma) (assuming available)
   - attach_task_profile shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha
   - confirm_candidate_preparedness shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha

But note: shift_candidate_beta already has candidate_transport_leg_linked transport_leg_alpha (init) and candidate_loading_container_linked loading_container_beta (init). Good.

Now we need to link operator and skill certificate and compliance certificate to shift_candidate_beta:

- assign_operator_resource shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, operator_available driver_operator_alpha)
- assign_skill_certificate shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha (requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, skill_certificate_available skill_certificate_alpha)
- assign_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha (requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha)

Now we need to load/unload payload at origin and destination.

But before loading, we need origin_availability_node_linked and destination_availability_node_linked (already true from init). Also need candidate_prepared and candidate_task_profile_linked (we will have after prep).

Thus:

- load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   Precondition: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (true after step1), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true), cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha (true), not origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha (currently false). So ok.

Effect: origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha true, origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha true, origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha true, cargo_available false.

- unload_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   Precondition: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (true), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true after attach), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true), origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha (true after load), origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha (true), not origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha (currently false). So ok.

Effect: origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha true, origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha true, cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true, not origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha.

Now we have origin_node_ready true, origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true.

Now do same for destination:

- load_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   Precondition: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha (true after step2), destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha (true), cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha (true), not destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha (currently false). So ok.

Effect: destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha true, destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha true, destination_payload_linked destination_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha true, cargo_available false.

- unload_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   Precondition: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha (true), candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true after attach), destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha (true), destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha (true), destination_payload_linked destination_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha (true), not destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha